        "value": "Cora (McCallum et al., 2000), Citeseer (Sen et al., 2008), and Pubmed (Yang et al., 2016) are among the most widely used benchmark datasets for the semi-supervised node classification. These are citation networks, where nodes, edges, features, and labels respectively correspond to papers, undirected paper citations, the bag-of-words representations of papers, and the academic topics of papers.",
        "start_char_doc": 77039,
        "end_char_doc": 77435,
        "prefix": "course, staff, and faculty. *",
        "suffix": "**The Synthetic Cora Network** The",
        "valueSource": "extracted"
      },
