      },
      "schema:description": {
        "value": "We use the synthetic dataset, called cSBMs (Deshpande et al., 2018), to demonstrate the mitigation of oversmoothing. This synthetic data is an undirected graph representing 100 nodes in a two-dimensional space with two classes randomly connected with a probability of $p = 0.9$. We report the layer-wise Dirichlet energy given a GNN of 40 layers.",
